     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Sample Space:</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A heart</td>\n<td>A spade</td>\n<td>A club</td>\n<td>A diamond</td>\n<td>K spade</td>\n<td>K club</td>\n<td>Q heart</td>\n<td>Q spade</td>\n<td>J heart</td>\n<td>J spade</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>These are mutually exclusive.</p>\n<p>There are 10 cards.</p>\n<p>You can use the Addition Rule for Mutually Exclusive Events:</p>\n<p>If <span data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span data-math=\"F\"></span> are mutually exclusive events, then <span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {E\\,{\\text{or}}\\,F} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ P}}\\left( E \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ P}}\\left( F \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>There are 4 Aces and 2 kings.</p>\n<p>P(A or K) = <span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{{10}} + \\frac{2}{{10}} = \\frac{6}{{10}} = \\frac{3}{5}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{5}\">\\frac{3}{5}</span>"
    }
